       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day (800 mg four times daily) in a monitored setting. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg** PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg** PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg** PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and any note to add (for example \"take with food\"), and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg per dose really is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly, and I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
